 "extract": "The Eurasian chaffinch, common chaffinch,  or simply the chaffinch (Fringilla coelebs) is a common and widespread small passerine bird –  in the finch family. The male is brightly coloured with a blue-grey cap and rust-red underparts. The female is more subdued in colouring, but both sexes have two contrasting white wing bars and white sides to the tail. The male bird has a strong voice and sings from exposed perches to attract a mate.",
